# Xbox Wireless Controller / Elite Series 2 over Bluetooth.
#
# The Bluetooth HID descriptor includes a keyboard collection for the Xbox and
# Share buttons, so udev's input_id classifier tags the pad ID_INPUT_KEYBOARD
# and never sets ID_INPUT_JOYSTICK. SDL2's udev backend enumerates only devices
# carrying that tag, so EmulationStation and RetroArch cannot see the pad at all
# - while the kernel is delivering perfectly good BTN_GAMEPAD/EV_ABS events.
# Over USB the descriptor is clean, it is classified correctly, and it works;
# hence the symptom "only works when plugged in".
#
# Must sort after 60-input-id.rules, which is what sets the tag being corrected.
#
# Two matches, deliberately. Xbox pads change product ID across firmware
# revisions (the One S 02e0 -> 02fd transition is the documented case), so
# pinning a PID means a routine firmware update silently un-fixes this with
# nothing in any log pointing here. Matching the name survives that. Keeping
# the PID match too means a name change does not un-fix it either. Both stay
# narrow: bus 0005 is Bluetooth and 045e is Microsoft, and no Microsoft
# keyboard or mouse reports the name below or that product ID.

ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="input", \
  ATTRS{id/bustype}=="0005", ATTRS{id/vendor}=="045e", \
  ATTRS{name}=="Xbox Wireless Controller", \
  ENV{ID_INPUT_JOYSTICK}="1"

ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="input", \
  ATTRS{id/bustype}=="0005", ATTRS{id/vendor}=="045e", ATTRS{id/product}=="0b22", \
  ENV{ID_INPUT_JOYSTICK}="1"
